{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzhwFk3m7r5sJsdsJRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":778,"cache_read_input_tokens":23521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":778},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"594863ab-9c7f-46a0-9240-feb852d96e19","uuid":"491e1ea6-d892-41bb-8890-786062e1a114","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:00:58.366Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzhvzNYYuJaJCmcnBMe","thinking_duration_ms":2147,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzhwFk3m7r5sJsdsJRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016XZzQhZxDQoZiS9Ackm3pE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-DKBZV5; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import time\\n\",\"import time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"    return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\",\"    # DynamoDB rejects float; keep the score a Decimal.\\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_second_publish_stores_similar(self):\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"A\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"cron twice\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"B\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"cron once\"})\n        self.assertEqual(stored[\"similar\"][0][\"slug\"], \"first-story\")\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nopen('ANSWER.md','w').write('''# Cause\n\n`similarity()` returns a Python `float`, and `publish()` stores those scores in\nthe item's `similar` list. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats\n(`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`).\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty, so `similar` was `[]`\nand no float was ever written. From the second publish on, `similar` holds\nscores, so `put_item` fails and the handler returns 500.\n\n# Fix\n\n`similarity()` in `src/app.py` now returns `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`.\n\nTo keep it from coming back, I added `test_second_publish_stores_similar` in\n`tests/test_publish.py`. It publishes two stories, so the `similar` path runs.\nThe fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does. The old test only published\none story into an empty table, which is why it never caught this.\n''')\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":778,"cache_read_input_tokens":23521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":778},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"594863ab-9c7f-46a0-9240-feb852d96e19","uuid":"0677e56c-ab4c-47e4-9f4b-2717cf82d6ca","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:01:02.538Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzhvzNYYuJaJCmcnBMe","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016XZzQhZxDQoZiS9Ackm3pE":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-DKBZV5; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import time\\n\",\"import time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"    return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\",\"    # DynamoDB rejects float; keep the score a Decimal.\\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_second_publish_stores_similar(self):\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"A\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"cron twice\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"B\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"cron once\"})\n        self.assertEqual(stored[\"similar\"][0][\"slug\"], \"first-story\")\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nopen('ANSWER.md','w').write('''# Cause\n\n`similarity()` returns a Python `float`, and `publish()` stores those scores in\nthe item's `similar` list. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats\n(`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`).\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty, so `similar` was `[]`\nand no float was ever written. From the second publish on, `similar` holds\nscores, so `put_item` fails and the handler returns 500.\n\n# Fix\n\n`similarity()` in `src/app.py` now returns `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`.\n\nTo keep it from coming back, I added `test_second_publish_stores_similar` in\n`tests/test_publish.py`. It publishes two stories, so the `similar` path runs.\nThe fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does. The old test only published\none story into an empty table, which is why it never caught this.\n''')\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -4"}}}
