{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzigu52MiersRPQb7Y8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because the `similar` scores are Python floats, and DynamoDB rejects floats. I've fixed it, and both tests now pass. I haven't deployed anything.\n\n- **Cause:** `similarity()` in `src/app.py` returns a float, and `publish()` stores those scores in the item's `similar` list. boto3 raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` on `put_item`, so the handler returns 500.\n- **Why only the second publish:** the first publish found an empty table, so `similar` was `[]` and no float was ever written. From the second publish on, there are scores to store.\n- **Fix:** `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`.\n- **Regression test:** I added `test_second_publish_stores_similar`, which publishes two stories in a row. The old test only published one story into an empty table, so it never reached this path. The fake table already rejects floats the way boto3 does, so the new test fails if floats come back.\n\nThe cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1009,"cache_read_input_tokens":24299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1009},"output_tokens":353,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"594863ab-9c7f-46a0-9240-feb852d96e19","uuid":"e9ab1700-29dc-47d7-8b04-abdd702a013b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:01:06.617Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzigevwArVB7tiAs3nG"}
